------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Presentations of groups
--
-- More stored matrices of local circuits, as literals
--
-- As GeneralN.Locals (whose literals the proofs here reuse), for the
-- singly controlled ZX and XZ on the wires 0 1, read on three wires.
-- A chain of literal products may have at most four or so factors: its
-- final refl evaluates the product without sharing, 8 ^ (d − 1) paths
-- per entry for d factors (seven blew 5 GB), so Z on wire 0, spelled
-- through the swap, is proved first on its own (`mid-def`).
-- The literal proofs go through the words spelled at width 3: under
-- ↓ᵏ the gates are not syntactically those of the literals, and the
-- conversion checker would then compare the two readings by evaluating;
-- and every factor without a literal has its reading given explicitly,
-- an unsolved one making the final comparison evaluate a product with a
-- metavariable in it.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

